From: Tiago Damascena <tiagobdamascena@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] One option per pad, BUTTON LAYOUT; preferred player 1 by default (RelicOS)

Asked on the device (M22 build 22): why three button options? Whether a
pad's letters are known is the right question, and the answer is that
RelicOS never really knows them -- SDL names positions (a = south) and
learns letters only for Nintendo-brand pads; a PlayStation pad has
none. The only real choice is which position confirms, and those who
move A also move X: the two layouts are mirror images.

So the map is kept by POSITION for every pad -- SDL is told not to use
button labels, and the table's SNES swap applies to all (the internal
pad keeps x/y as SDL gives them, its BTN_X being the top button) -- and
each pad has one option, BUTTON LAYOUT: NINTENDO (A right, B bottom,
the default on every pad, this handheld's own) or XBOX / PLAYSTATION
(A bottom, B right), mirroring the four at lookup time
(InputConfig::relicosName) and in relicos-pads. The labels/swap_ab/
swap_xy keys of the previous page are gone.

PREFERRED PLAYER 1 gets the rule asked for: on for the handheld by
default; turned off there, a connected pad comes first; on for an
external pad, that pad, one at a time (controllers.player1 = "",
"external" or a GUID). One-line description.
